Subject: [PATCH] vayu_wifi W25: WPA2-PSK 4-way handshake, WMI key install, HTT data path, en0 (PMK from a file)

Base: the W24G research source (/mnt/ramdisk/wifi-work2, 2026-11-02 04:59): the eight W22..W24
files (vayu_wifi_smmu/ce_wire/htc/ce/htc_connect/wmi/scan/sta.c + their sys/ headers) were copied
into the test26 tree unchanged and this diff is relative to them.  bsd/conf/files is relative to
the test26 base (/mnt/ramdisk/n13c/src, branch vayu-test26 d15caf0).

What W24 left: passive scan OK (54 beacons, 41 BSSIDs), auth status 0, assoc status 0 aid 2,
HTT in-order RX delivering the EAPOL-Key 1/4 frames (len 131 = 24+8+99, decap 1, from DS), and a
panic in __doprnt from eapol_key() when the line still used %s (fixed in W24G).

The PMK never travels in a boot argument (boot arguments are logged by the loader, the kernel,
launchd's kern.bootargs and a panic buffer).  It is read from the root volume:
/private/etc/vayu-wifi/gunwest.pmk, 64 hex digits and one line, mode 0600, when the handshake arms
(vnode_lookup + vnode_getattr + vn_rdwr, as vayu_pas.c reads /fw), and only with the boot argument
vayu_wifi_pmk_file=1.  The buffer is wiped after the parse; the only line is
"vayu-wifi: W25 S0 pmk: OK file (len 32)" (or ERROR with no secret).  PMK/PTK/KCK/KEK/TK/GTK and
nonces never reach the log.  To put the file into an existing root image:
/tmp/opencode/ds-wifi-addfile.sh IN.apfs OUT.apfs gunwest.pmk /private/etc/vayu-wifi/gunwest.pmk
(tools/apfs/apfs.py takes the image apart, tools/apfs/mkapfs.py lays it out again; the file is read
back out and compared before it exits 0).

Changes:
 - bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_rsn.c/.h (new): the 4-way handshake.  Crypto through libkern's provider
   (osfmk/minicrypto registers at EARLY_BOOT): g_crypto_funcs->cchmac_fn + ccsha1_di for HMAC-SHA1,
   ccaes_ecb_decrypt for RFC 3394 unwrap; one self-test (RFC 2202 HMAC-SHA1, RFC 3394 vector)
   before any use.  PRF-SHA1 for the 384-bit PTK, message 2/4 with the assoc RSN IE and MIC under
   the KCK, message 3/4 MIC checked + GTK KDE unwrapped, message 4/4 in the clear, then
   WMI_VDEV_INSTALL_KEY (0x5009, TLV 0x60) pairwise index 0 and group (KDE index), and
   WMI_PEER_SET_PARAM (0x6004) AUTHORIZE.
 - bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_net.c/.h (new): Ethernet <-> native wifi, en0 attached with the BSD interface
   KPI through hakios_net_attach() (wireless link, up only after the keys), RX MSDUs to
   hakios_net_input(), TX from the interface's thread to HTT; a minimal DHCP client plus ARP and
   one ICMP echo to the router behind vayu_wifi_dhcp=1; the station boundary (hakios_sta_ops) is
   filled so Apple80211 requests have answers.
 - bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_scan.c: HTT data TX (H2T_TX_FRM, 20+52-byte message, frame in a 64x2048 TX
   pool, frag-bank entry per slot, TX_COMPL_IND 0x07 frees slots), EAPOL and data frames handed to
   the handshake/net paths, EAPOL diagnostic limited to the first 8 frames.
 - bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_sta.c: PEER_ASSOC (PEER_FLAG_AUTH|NEED_PTK_4WAY, assoc RSN IE) and VDEV_UP
   after the association, the handshake window, en0 up, a 20 s data window (or 180 s with
   vayu_wifi_keep=1), then VDEV_DOWN/PEER_DELETE/VDEV_STOP.  Stage lines: "vayu-wifi: W25 S<n> ...".
 - bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_htc_connect.c: the HTT TX buffer is 128 bytes (the TX message is 72), stage
   line S1 after the scan.
 - bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_smmu.c: redwood_smmu_lock -> hakios_smmu_lock (the name in the test26 tree).

Verification done on the host: build rc=2 (the usual export-check/symbolset failure, the kernel
links), the W25 strings are in the kernel, host test of the exact aes_unwrap/prf_sha1 code against
RFC 3394 and RFC 2202 vectors (after fixing the A^t half-word offset), and the add-file tool
round-trips the 4 MiB work/hackios-vayu/userland/root.apfs (the added file reads back mode 0600
uid 0).  Not yet run on the phone.

